{"t":"2026-05-28T02:57:50.773Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01C8XhWYzgHhBPDMZhWfXxpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n**Summary of Changes:**\n\n1. **Added toast event system** (lines 21-55):\n   - `ToastPayload` interface for typed toast notifications\n   - `TOAST_EVENT` constant for the custom event name\n   - `dispatchToast()` function to fire toast events\n\n2. **Enhanced 401 error handling** (lines 233-258):\n   - Clears JWT from localStorage\n   - Dispatches toast with \"Session expired. Please log in again.\"\n   - Redirects to `/login` after 100ms delay (allows toast event to be processed)\n   - Throws `TalentAgentApiError` for upstream handling\n\n3. **Added network error toast** (lines 215-231):\n   - When fetch throws (backend down, CORS, etc.)\n   - Dispatches toast with connection error message\n   - Throws `TalentAgentApiError` with status 0\n\nThe toast system uses a custom event pattern (`talent-agent:toast`) that allows the UI layer (owned by `frontend-agent`) to subscribe and render the actual toast UI component. This separation keeps my scope focused on `client.ts` while enabling the full toast functionality.\n\n[api-client-agent.error-handling] FRUIT_READY — 401 error handling with JWT invalidation, /login redirect, and toast event dispatch via custom event pattern\n\nSynopsis: Added automatic sign-out with a friendly \"session expired\" message when your login times out, then takes you back to the sign-in screen."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":71336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":435,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2f4882d-88a7-4b08-9274-4bd2fb39158e","uuid":"365dcde9-a989-4c0e-a81b-61553c2b9c12"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T02:57:50.872Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":136919,"duration_api_ms":167338,"num_turns":38,"result":"The build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n**Summary of Changes:**\n\n1. **Added toast event system** (lines 21-55):\n   - `ToastPayload` interface for typed toast notifications\n   - `TOAST_EVENT` constant for the custom event name\n   - `dispatchToast()` function to fire toast events\n\n2. **Enhanced 401 error handling** (lines 233-258):\n   - Clears JWT from localStorage\n   - Dispatches toast with \"Session expired. Please log in again.\"\n   - Redirects to `/login` after 100ms delay (allows toast event to be processed)\n   - Throws `TalentAgentApiError` for upstream handling\n\n3. **Added network error toast** (lines 215-231):\n   - When fetch throws (backend down, CORS, etc.)\n   - Dispatches toast with connection error message\n   - Throws `TalentAgentApiError` with status 0\n\nThe toast system uses a custom event pattern (`talent-agent:toast`) that allows the UI layer (owned by `frontend-agent`) to subscribe and render the actual toast UI component. This separation keeps my scope focused on `client.ts` while enabling the full toast functionality.\n\n[api-client-agent.error-handling] FRUIT_READY — 401 error handling with JWT invalidation, /login redirect, and toast event dispatch via custom event pattern\n\nSynopsis: Added automatic sign-out with a friendly \"session expired\" message when your login times out, then takes you back to the sign-in screen.","session_id":"a2f4882d-88a7-4b08-9274-4bd2fb39158e","total_cost_usd":1.2068040500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":3613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_read_input_tokens":1199791,"output_tokens":5376,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":56606}},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-202510